SCHEMA_INSUFFICIENT: The schema lacks predicates to encode two critical spatial concepts from this rule: (1) "between a safety zone and the adjacent curb" — there is no predicate for being in the space between a zone boundary and the adjacent curb (the available `in_zone` only captures being inside the zone itself, not the area between the zone and curb), and (2) "within 30 feet of the ends of a safety zone" — there is no predicate or function for distance specifically to the ends/endpoints of a safety zone (the available `dist_to_feature` with `PF_SafetyZone` measures general proximity to the safety zone feature, not distance from its longitudinal endpoints). The diagnostic feedback explicitly identifies these as the semantic gaps that caused the previous encoding to fail, and no combination of existing schema predicates can distinguish these spatial concepts from general zone proximity.